    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Mebendazole (Emverm) label:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " roundworm dose: 1 tablet morning and evening for 3 consecutive days. Same schedule for adults and children two years and older; the tablet may be chewed, swallowed or crushed and mixed w food. Not cured three wks after tx: a second course is advised. CI: known hypersensitivity to the drug or its excipients. Convulsions reported in infants < 1 y. Agranulocytosis and neutropenia at higher doses or longer durations than recommended: monitor blood counts then. SJS/TEN reported w mebendazole + metronidazole: ⍉ the combo."
     }
    ]
   }
  ]
 },
